---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe28.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — Three Distinct Categories of Change" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Accounting Policy Changes" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Changes in Accounting Estimates — Prospective Application" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Distinguishing a Policy Change From an Estimate Change" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Correction of Prior Period Errors — Retrospective Restatement" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Materiality of an Error" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — a Voluntary Accounting Policy Change" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Correcting a Material Prior Period Error" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IAS 8" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 会计政策、会计估计变更和差错更正 · Converged with IAS 8 · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Three genuinely different treatments for three genuinely different situations</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 28 governs HOW an enterprise ACCOUNTS for CHANGES in ACCOUNTING policies, CHANGES in ACCOUNTING estimates, and CORRECTIONS of PRIOR period ERRORS — THREE genuinely DIFFERENT situations, EACH requiring a DIFFERENT accounting TREATMENT, CLOSELY converged with IAS 8 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Three Distinct Categories of Change</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Policy changes, estimate changes, and error corrections</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Treatment</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Accounting policy change</span><span>RETROSPECTIVE application (RESTATING comparatives), UNLESS a NEW standard's OWN transition provisions SPECIFY otherwise</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Accounting estimate change</span><span>PROSPECTIVE application (NO restatement of PRIOR periods)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Prior period error correction</span><span>RETROSPECTIVE restatement, for MATERIAL errors</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Accounting Policy Changes</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Required by a new standard, or voluntary for more reliable information</div><div class="text-supporting">A CHANGE in ACCOUNTING policy is PERMITTED WHERE REQUIRED by a NEW or REVISED accounting STANDARD, or WHERE the CHANGE will RESULT in the financial STATEMENTS providing MORE RELIABLE and MORE RELEVANT information ABOUT the effects of TRANSACTIONS — a VOLUNTARY change is APPLIED retrospectively, AS IF the NEW policy had ALWAYS been APPLIED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Changes in Accounting Estimates — Prospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Adjusting future periods only, with no restatement</div><div class="text-supporting">A CHANGE in an ACCOUNTING estimate (e.g. a REVISED useful LIFE for a FIXED asset, or a REVISED bad DEBT allowance RATE) is APPLIED PROSPECTIVELY — AFFECTING the CURRENT period and FUTURE periods ONLY, WITH NO restatement of PRIOR periods, since the ORIGINAL estimate was REASONABLE based on the INFORMATION available AT the time.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Distinguishing a Policy Change From an Estimate Change</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A key judgement with materially different consequences</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE it is DIFFICULT to DISTINGUISH a CHANGE in ACCOUNTING policy FROM a CHANGE in ACCOUNTING estimate, the CHANGE is TREATED as a CHANGE in ESTIMATE — a PRACTICAL default REFLECTING that MOST such AMBIGUOUS cases GENUINELY involve a REFINEMENT of JUDGEMENT RATHER than a WHOLESALE change in the UNDERLYING accounting PRINCIPLE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Correction of Prior Period Errors — Retrospective Restatement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Restating comparatives as if the error never occurred</div><div class="text-supporting">MATERIAL errors RELATING to PRIOR periods are CORRECTED retrospectively — RESTATING the COMPARATIVE amounts PRESENTED for the PRIOR period(s) in WHICH the ERROR occurred, AS IF the ERROR had NEVER been MADE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Materiality of an Error</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Only material errors require retrospective correction</div><div class="text-supporting">ONLY MATERIAL errors REQUIRE retrospective RESTATEMENT — an ERROR is MATERIAL if it COULD reasonably be EXPECTED to INFLUENCE the ECONOMIC decisions of USERS relying on the FINANCIAL statements, ASSESSED both INDIVIDUALLY and IN aggregate WITH other errors.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — a Voluntary Accounting Policy Change</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Restating comparatives for improved reliability</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Changing an inventory cost formula</div><div class="wk-body">A company changes its inventory cost formula from FIFO to weighted average, determining this provides more reliable and relevant information about its inventory costs given a change in its purchasing pattern.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company APPLIES the NEW weighted AVERAGE formula RETROSPECTIVELY, RESTATING comparative FIGURES as IF weighted AVERAGE had ALWAYS been USED, DISCLOSING the NATURE and REASON for the CHANGE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Correcting a Material Prior Period Error</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Restating a comparative period to remove the error</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A previously omitted liability</div><div class="wk-body">A company discovers that a material RMB 10,000,000 liability was mistakenly omitted from the prior year's financial statements due to a clerical error.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company RESTATES the PRIOR year'S comparative FIGURES to INCLUDE the RMB 10,000,000 liability (and its ASSOCIATED expense), CORRECTING the error RETROSPECTIVELY, WITH appropriate DISCLOSURE of the NATURE of the error and the AMOUNT of the CORRECTION.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 28 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and reason for any accounting policy change, and its financial effect</span><span>Nature and amount of any change in accounting estimate affecting the current or future periods</span><span>Nature of any prior period error corrected, and the amount of the correction for each period presented</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Distinguishing a genuine accounting policy change from a change in estimate</span><span>Assessing whether an identified error is material</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Quantifying the financial effect of a policy change or error correction on prior periods</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 8</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 28 vs IAS 8</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 28</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 8</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Policy changes</span><span>Retrospective</span><span>Retrospective — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Estimate changes</span><span>Prospective</span><span>Prospective — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Error corrections</span><span>Retrospective restatement</span><span>Retrospective restatement — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, with NO meaningful SUBSTANTIVE divergence to REPORT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every category of change lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Policy change / error correction</span><span>ALL comparative statements</span><span>Retrospectively restated</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Estimate change</span><span>Current and future periods only</span><span>No restatement of prior periods</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 30</span><span>Presentation of Financial Statements — governs the overall comparative presentation this Standard's restatement provisions affect</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Retrospective application</div><div class="glossary-def">Applying a new accounting policy or correcting an error as if it had always applied, restating comparative periods accordingly.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Prospective application</div><div class="glossary-def">Applying a change only to the current and future periods, without restating prior periods.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe28 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
